Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-09-2001||06:31 PM||||Im taking apart my sisters car, which my dad gave her, after he bought a new car 4 himself.<P><BR>Its a ford topaz, and it has those automatic seatbelts.  The driver side doesn't work.  I took the motor apart and the brushes are bad on it.<P>I went to radio shack and they dont carry brushes, but do carry little motors.  A bit suprised that RS dont carry brushes.  I was wondering where i can get brushes from.  I dont want to go to the junkyard yet to pull one from another car, its a pain in the ass to remove the motors.  I might try the hobby shop, or see if one from my rc car will fit.<P>I noticed a lot of motors wear out, or dont work because the brushes get dirty or just turn into dust.  Like alternators. And theres no Brushes R US Retail store.||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||10-09-2001||06:46 PM||||Any good electric motor rebuild shop should have a big enough selection of brushes to fill your needs.Or you could ask your local automotive electric rebuilder.||||reg||14
Z||000002||theogre||10-09-2001||08:53 PM||||get the motor from the passengers side of another car. You may be able to use the thing whole. At the least you can use it for parts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
